analysis.originalLogic:
In `TOFinder::process_assign`, when an assignment was `lhs = Not(place)`, the threader transferred conditions known on `lhs` back to `place` by inverting polarity with `Condition::inv`, which swapped `Polarity::Eq` and `Polarity::Ne`. The removed helper was:
```
fn inv(mut self) -> Self {
    self.polarity = match self.polarity {
        Polarity::Eq => Polarity::Ne,
        Polarity::Ne => Polarity::Eq,
    };
    self
}
```
and the old branch used:
```
let conds = conditions.map(self.arena, Condition::inv);
```
This treats `!a ?= v` as `a ?= !v` only when values are one bit wide. The patch's comment states: `// Constructing the conditions by inverting the polarity` `// of equality is only correct for bools.`
